## 16. Completion Criteria

The milestone is complete only when:

1. The backend can analyze previously extracted document content.
2. Actual images can be analyzed using a vision-capable model.
3. User stories and acceptance criteria are understood.
4. Requirements are converted into a consistent URS.
5. Requirements preserve their source references.
6. Duplicate candidates are identified.
7. Conflicts are detected and preserved.
8. Missing information is identified.
9. The URS can be retrieved and reviewed through the frontend.
10. Users can edit requirements and resolve conflicts.
11. Approval restrictions work correctly.
12. Existing functionality remains operational.
13. Relevant automated tests pass.

At completion, provide:
- Architecture changes.
- Files created and modified.
- New API endpoints.
- Database changes.
- AI models and configurations used.
- Tests executed and results.
- Known limitations.
- Features remaining for the next milestone.

Do not claim any functionality is complete unless it has actually been implemented and tested.
